  "description": "Canon \u00a76 regular, Gate A \u00a77.3: the delivery-mission takeover. Screensavers blank, the three devices warm up, then map (left) / typewriter briefing (centre) / cargo plate (right), and the tracking-page deadpan runs its course. Every word is drawn from a pool; the countdown is drawn as a WHOLE SEQUENCE (pickIndex + columns) because which stop it stalls at and which excuse lands only make sense together. Source: the S01-E00 Loop Scenes outline, 'Delivery Monitor Loops'. TEST CONTENT (2026-09-02, Josh): the pools are placeholder copy sized to exercise the system and the repetition audit, NOT signed writing. Expect them to be rewritten as the experience is refined; nothing here is load-bearing except the shapes (a countdown is one row, a report is a topic plus its body). ART1 (2026-09-11) added the equipment track canon \u00a74 always wanted: the HAM receiver's amber window comes up WITH the relay wake and falls back to dark as the takeover closes. It was missing on purpose until now \u2014 ENV-005 did not exist, so there was no equipment target to name (#10).",
